<settings>
    <servers>
        <server>
            <id>my-repo</id>
            <username>your-username</username>
            <password>your-password</password>
        </server>
    </servers>
</settings>
Running the Command:
After setting up your pom.xml and settings.xml, you can run the mvn clean deploy command in your terminal from the root directory of your Maven project.
This will build your project and deploy the resulting artifacts to the specified remote repository.

Note:
Make sure you have the necessary permissions to deploy to the specified repository, and ensure that your project is properly configured to avoid any deployment issues.
